  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123309,
      "SummaryText": "Objective:\nThe purpose of this 2025 RMP Resubmission is to update the ARLANXEO, USA LLC, Orange Site RMP information in compliance with the EPA 40 CFR Part 68 Risk Management Planning requirement to update the RMP data every five years.\n\nFacility:\nThe ARLANXEO, USA LLC, Orange site is located in the industrial chemical road, Farm Road 1006 of Orange, Texas. The facility had four operating units, Cobalt Butadiene Rubber (CoBR), Lithium Butadiene Rubber (LiBR), EPR (Keltan) and Therban Rubber manufacturing units, until closure of the EPDM (Keltan) manufacturing unit on May 10, 2020. Therefore, the site now has three manufacturing units supported by a common Utilities department.\nThe site now produces three basic types of polymerized synthetic rubber with variations of each type. These include two different types of polybutadiene rubber and hydrogenated nitrile butadiene rubber. The synthetic rubber produced from the site is used by customers to fabricate consumer products such as tires, hoses, timing belts and several automotive parts. The Utilities area of the plant supplies water, steam, electricity, compressed air, cooling water, potable water, process water and refrigeration for the polybutadiene production units. The Orange site Utilities department also supplies steam to a neighbor Chevron Chemical plant.\nHydrocarbons are used as monomers and solvents in the units. ARLANXEO, USA LLC, Orange Plant inventories all the hydrocarbons used in the plant. There are now two hydrocarbons and two chemicals that are used in quantities above the threshold quantities as defined in EPA 40 CFR Part 68 Risk Management Planning regulation. The hydrocarbons are 1,3-butadiene and 1-butene. The other two chemicals are chlorine and anhydrous ammonia, which are primarily used in the Utilities department. \nThe ARLANXEO, USA LLC, Orange, Texas site supports many outreach programs for the community including, the United Way, Organizational Health Committee, and supports other local progr"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123309,
      "SummaryText": "ams. The facility maintains RC 14001 and ISO 14001 certifications.\n\nRecent Changes and Improvements:\nThe increase in rail cars on site for 1,3-Butadiene raw material has raised the potential maximum inventory of this chemical to 5,400,000 lbs. The rail car supply is intended to supplement 1,3-Butadiene raw material supply when there are constraints in the existing pipeline supply. In addition, the rail cars will be unloaded into the existing 1,3-Butadiene storage spheres, with each rail car containing approximately 160,000 lbs of 1,3-Butadiene. There is no increase to the tank farm storage capacity.\nBoiler #5 installation project was completed in 2021.\n\nProcess Safety and Risk Management:\nThe ARLANXEO, USA LLC, Orange Plant is a PSM covered site. It complies with the OSHA PSM Regulation 29 CFR 1910.119 and EPA 40 CFR Part 68 Risk Management Planning regulations. All the manufacturing units comply with the fourteen PSM elements and, except for Therban unit (which is not RMP-covered), are considered to be Program Level III processes under Risk Management Planning.\n\nThe site PSM programs include:\nEmployee Participation\nProcess Safety Information\nProcess Hazard Analyses\nOperating Procedures\nEmployee Training\nContractor Safety\nPre-Start Up Safety Review\nMechanical Integrity\nSafe work Practices\nManagement of Change\nIncident Investigation\nEmergency Planning and Response\nCompliance Audits\nTrade Secrets\n\nAccidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies:\nRelease Prevention:\nHandling of hazardous materials undergoes a rigorous process hazard analysis review. The site maintains a Management of Change (MOC) program across the plant with updated procedures, incident and near hit reporting, preventive and corrective actions, and tracking of action items to closure. The site also maintains a mechanical integrity program for equipment, piping and vessel inspections, testing and repairs.\nMaintenance and improvement of Health, Safety and Environmental systems are ongoing"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 2,
      "FacilityID": 1000123309,
